ye on the  horizon line and watch for falling trees  and structures to get one up on the  opposition another thing to consider  with materials in general is what items  give you the most resources or the  quickest resources pallets rock  formations huge pine trees and the  beasts trees at moisty are great to get  out your axe and just smack a few  different things as you walk past you  may find something which yields more  materials than you expect it there's a  small glitch that can be used when  gathering materials ax switching or axe  cancelling if you prefer it works best  on the PC but with practice it's pretty  good on consult  to do it begin to mine like usual but  after your first swing hits switch to  your inventory items and immediately  switch back again and start the process  all over your character will definitely  look like they're having a seizure but  with practice you can obliterate  anything using axe canceling let's look  at our building options during fights  when climbing high it's a good idea to  put a ramp over your head to protect you  from head shots from a higher distance  this is also the case with rubes which  can be placed above your head if the  opposition has the high ground you'd be  surprised how many players jump down and  give away that high ground once they  feel they can't get debris shots  depending on the material you choose to  build with you can peek through the  slots in the structure and get the drop  on your enemy for tonight is very  frustrating in that sense some gaps you  can shoot through some you can not in  here you are completely safe so peek  away a quick reminder about edit mode  edit your structures in particular the  walls and remove all the segments in  front of you you'll now be able to see  through to the other side and it acts  like a one-way mirror  speaking of editing tiles in Sniper  battles most people are looking for  someone to peek their head out of the  top mix it up a little by quickly  editing in a